  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a tree consisting of NNN nodes and N−1N-1N−1 edges. The iii-th node has value AiA_iAi​.\n\nLet d(x,y)d(x, y)d(x,y) denote the number of edges on the (unique) shortest path between xxx and yyy.\n\nFor each node u&nbsp;(1≤u≤N)u \\ (1 \\leq u \\leq N)u&nbsp;(1≤u≤N), compute the following quantity:\n\n∑i=1N⌊Ai2d(u,i)⌋\\sum_{i=1}^N \\left \\lfloor \\frac{A_i}{2^{d(u, i)}} \\right\\rfloori=1∑N​⌊2d(u,i)Ai​​⌋Here, ⌊&nbsp;⌋\\left\\lfloor \\ \\right\\rfloor⌊&nbsp;⌋ denotes the floor function.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the number of nodes in the tree.\nThe next N−1N-1N−1 lines describe the edges. The iii-th of these N−1N-1N−1 lines contains two space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting an edge between uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​.\nThe next line contains NNN space separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line NNN space-separated integers, the iii-th of which denotes the answer for node iii.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤5⋅1041 \\leq N \\leq 5\\cdot 10^41≤N≤5⋅104",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "1≤Ai≤1061 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^61≤Ai​≤106.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 5⋅1045\\cdot 10^45⋅104."
    ],
